From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] Add texture-backed static grain after blur

Generate a deterministic 1024x1024 grain lookup once per renderer and sample
it with the same bilinear/repeat approach used by production compositor and
post-processing implementations. This avoids float-hash precision artifacts
and the quantized cells that produced repeating vertical patterns at larger
grain sizes.

Apply one grain lookup after the final Dual-Kawase upsample and color
adjustments. The pattern is anchored to framebuffer pixels, so partial damage
redraws remain static and deterministic. The existing Dual-Kawase kernels are
left intact because their 8-tap weights match SceneFX, Hyprland, KWin, and the
FrostKiwi reference implementation.

